===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[Image:Clinching getting the back.jpg|thumb|right|(Sense 6) One [[wrestling|wrestler]] is trying to get the back.]]

# Any of several [[fastening]]s.
# The act or process of holding fast; that which serves to hold fast.
#: {{syn|en|grip|grasp}}
#: {{ux|en|to get a good '''clinch''' of an antagonist, or of a weapon}}
#: {{ux|en|to secure anything by a '''clinch'''}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[pun]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[hitch]] or [[bend]] by which a rope is made fast to the ring of an [[anchor]], or the [[breeching]] of a ship's gun to the [[ringbolt]]s.
# A [[passionate]] [[embrace]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Judith Arnold|title=Moondance|passage=More likely, he was letting her know that his visit this morning was not going to end in a '''clinch'''—or something steamier. It was going to be about sitting at a table, drinking coffee and talking.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/jun/25/matt-hancock-sex-cop-busted-clinch-health-secretary-hookups|title=Matt Hancock, the one-time sex cop now busted for a dodgy clinch|author=Marina Hyde|date=2021-06-25|work=The Guardian|passage=So, then, to the health secretary’s “steamy '''clinch'''” with Gina Coladangelo, the lobbyist and long-term friend he took on as an aide last year {{...|(though initially did not declare it), and who was subsequently given a paid non-executive directorship at the Department of Health.}}}}
# {{lb|en|wrestling|combat sports}} The act of one or both fighters holding onto the other to prevent being hit or engage in standup [[grapple|grappling]].
# {{lb|en|slang|archaic}} A [[prison]] [[sentence]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1882|author=Henry Herman; Henry Arthur Jones|title=The Silver King
|passage=COOMBE: He got the '''clinch''' only last week — eighteen months. You see it's no good having anybody here as ain't got a unblemished character. We don't want to have the bluebottles come sniffing round here, do we?}}

